  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AMPLIFYING ASIAN ELEPHANT CONSERVATION THROUGH CAPACITY BUILDING AND SENSITIZATION PROGRAMS IN TAMIL NADU, INDIA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE GOAL OF THIS PROJECT IS TO ENSURE THE LONG-TERM SURVIVAL OF ASIAN ELEPHANT POPULATIONS BY MINIMIZING HUMAN-ELEPHANT CONFLICT (HEC) AND PROMOTE THE PEACEFUL SURVIVAL OF BOTH ELEPHANTS AND HUMANS IN TAMIL NADU, INDIA. THE PROJECT WILL CONDUCT HEC CAPACITY BUILDING TRAINING FOR FRONTLINE FOREST STAFF AND TO ADMINISTER HUMAN-ELEPHANT COEXISTENCE (HECX) SENSITIZATION PROGRAMS FOR MEDIA AND GOVERNMENT STAFF IN SATHYAMANGALAM TIGER RESERVE AND THE RECENTLY DECLARED SRIVILLIPUTHUR-MEGAMALAI TIGER RESERVE. IN PARTNERSHIP WITH THE TAMIL NADU FOREST DEPARTMENT, THE RECIPIENT WILL CONDUCT TRAININGS AND WORKSHOPS FOR FRONTLINE FOREST STAFF, FOREST RANGE OFFICERS, AND NEWLY HIRED PARK STAFF, JOURNALISTS, LAWYERS, LOCAL POLICE, AND OTHER STAKEHOLDERS IN BOTH PROTECTED AREAS. SPECIFIC ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: (1) CONDUCT TWO TWO-DAY TRAINING PROGRAMS FOR 60 FRONTLINE STAFF ON HEC AND HEC MITIGATION (2) CONDUCT TWO ONE-DAY SENSITIZATION PROGRAMS FOR 50 PARTICIPANTS, INCLUDING JOURNALISTS, LAWYERS, LOCAL POLICE, AND OTHER FOREST DEPARTMENT STAFF AND (3) EVALUATION OF THE IMPACTS OF THE TWO PROGRAMS AND CREATION OF A COMMUNICATION NETWORK AMONG PARTICIPANTS FOR INFORMATION SHARING.</narrative>
  </description>
